; pivot-mint.fk — the door pivot-coverage.bml named as the open stone (R24):
; turn one corpus row's fresh word into the exact source text of its pivot
; lexicon row in nl-lexicon-data.fk. PURE — string in, string out, no disk.
;
;   pivot-mint(mid, en, id) -> "            (list \"m<mid>\" \"gas\" \"<en>\" \"<id>\")\n"
;
; the same 12-space-indent, one-row-per-line, trailing-newline shape as
; nl-lexicon-grow.fk's jlg-row, but symbol "m<mid>" (the corpus row's own
; meaning-id, not a sequential "c<i>") and phase "gas" (just-minted, not
; "water"). Template read literally off the five rows R12 already minted
; by hand (m1257..m1261 in nl-lexicon-data.fk); tests/pivot-mint-band.fk
; proves pivot-mint reproduces every one of them, character for character.
;
; WHY THIS CELL STOPS HERE, AND DOES NOT WRITE TO DISK:
; nl-lexicon-data.fk already has a second writer — nl-lexicon-grow.fk's
; grow-rows/jlg-emit-cell, the web/messages projector. jlg-emit-cell does
; not append: it re-emits the WHOLE file (header comment, the
; nlt-corpus-lexicon defn, every row) from a fresh walk of the json corpus,
; wholesale, via write_file_text. grow-rows only ever knows about the
; c<i> rows it just derived — it carries no memory of m<mid> rows, hand-
; appended or otherwise. So the danger pivot-coverage.bml names ("the two
; writers need one shape first") is not a call-graph collision — pivot-
; mint and grow-rows never call each other, so that half is trivially
; clean — it is a DATA collision: the day the projector's runner (named in
; nl-lexicon-grow.fk's header, scripts/grow_nl_lexicon.fk — not yet built)
; next regenerates the file, every m<mid> row written by any hand or door,
; this one included, is silently gone, because jlg-emit-cell never reads
; the file it is about to overwrite. That risk is not introduced by this
; cell; it already exists the moment a human hand-appends an m-row today.
; But building a disk-writing pivot-mint-append would make it easier to
; repeat the same unsafe act more often, not safer to repeat — so this
; cell mints TEXT only. The next stone, named and not built here (same
; words pivot-coverage.bml already used): grow-rows/jlg-emit-cell must
; read the file it is about to write, keep every m<mid> row it finds, and
; only then may an append door touch nl-lexicon-data.fk automatically.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk

(do
    (defn pm-q () "\"")
    (defn pm-qs (s) (str_concat (pm-q) (str_concat s (pm-q))))
    ;; pivot-mint: (mid, en, id) -> the row's exact source text, PURE.
    (defn pivot-mint (mid en id)
        (str_concat "            (list "
            (str_concat (pm-qs (str_concat "m" (int_to_str mid)))
            (str_concat " " (str_concat (pm-qs "gas")
            (str_concat " " (str_concat (pm-qs en)
            (str_concat " " (str_concat (pm-qs id) ")\n")))))))))
    0)
